Pinned semantics: in (1) the raise happens when the scope OPENS — before any read in the body executes, so the body read produces no output line at all. The message pluralizes mechanically: 'Replica lag over 1 seconds'. In (2) 'failover: false' is an explicit scope option that flips the default log-and-fallback behavior to raising. Error output is always the two-line pattern: error= line then message= line, exact strings.

